  "readme": "# Mimi node 102: restore one missing short voice cue\n\nScene10040043/node102 had a blank voice. Restore only vo_adv_mimi,advg_mimi_aiduchi, already registered. A single four-second original audio decode and independent signed DSP identify the complete cue at791.719–792.181375 seconds (full NCC0.901933; effective0.924100; strongest other Mimi0.193684). Both complete120-frame source reviews place this entirely inside node102, conservative common readable interval791.487–793.387. The burned-in Chinese subtitle changes before the native panel and is not used as its boundary.\n\nThe existing normal repair/install gates preserve all other fields, IDs, branches and ordering. Complete saved review/manifest/ownership checks,281 other formal guards and22 protected files pass. No original CSV, body/face, subjective listening, acoustic preview equivalence, saved continuous gameplay or whole-scene acceptance is claimed.\n\nThe first system-Python stage exited1 before any write with a JSONDecodeError. Its actual exception document is retained. A separate fresh held file is Git-exact and parses in Node and existing ARM Python3.11; six differing NUL bytes in the exception document are recorded, with cause unknown and failed raw bytes unavailable. The unchanged normal modules subsequently ran in that existing ARM interpreter; no parser shim/repair is used. The first readonly Node observation also hit its default maxBuffer; that tooling error and the explicitly bounded corrected observation are recorded separately.\n\nOnly compact metadata and the small audio PCM are archived. Source screenshots and original videos are retained locally without another copy.\n"
